      "writtenOn": "2022-10-19T16:35:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The headerjars and implementationjars are not the .impl module but rather outputs of the SdkLibrary module itself, why should .impl module impact the visibility of these output files?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1858,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 1858,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "a85d78cbc77c54832a6302a9097942cff931646a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c8390cb_5453acad",
        "filename": "java/sdk_library.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1858,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-19T17:28:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We restrict access to the \u003cX\u003e.impl library using visibility because we want to limit the number of places that can access the implementation library jas (even if it is just the headers jar) to only those that the developer specifies so that they can make sure that it is not being misused. By misused I mean attempting to build against the implementation API. That is dangerous for lots of reasons.\n\nThese outputs are functionally identical implementation library jars to those produced by \u003cX\u003e.impl and so need to be restricted in the same way and for the same reason.",
      "parentUuid": "25272d62_7930e150",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1858,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 1858,
        "endChar": 94
